# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# Allowed types:
#   feat     - A new feature or capability
#   fix      - A bug fix
#   refactor - Code restructuring without behavioral changes
#   perf     - Performance improvements
#   test     - Adding or correcting tests
#   docs     - Documentation updates
#   build    - Build system, toolchain, or external dependencies
#   ci       - CI configuration, workflows, or scripts
#   chore    - Maintenance tasks or general housekeeping
#
# Common scopes:
#   web, api, shared, auth, db, ai, rag, ui, config
#
# Guidelines:
#   - Subject: Imperative mood ("add", not "added"), lowercase, 72 characters max.
#   - Body: Explain the motivation and context. What problem is being solved?
#     Why was this approach chosen over alternatives?
#   - Footer: Reference tracking IDs (e.g., Closes #123) or breaking changes.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

